<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Jan net household savings up HUF 33.3 bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary Jan net household savings up HUF 33.3 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net household savings rose 33.3 billion in January to 2,415.9 billion forints ($13.9 billion), the National Bank of Hungary said on Friday.</p>
<p> (in billion forints)    Jan '97	 Dec '96	Jan' 96</p>
<p> Forint savings	    2,271.5	 2,250.0	1,774.0</p>
<p> Foreign currency	    478.9	   475.4	  447.0</p>
<p> Total savings	     2,750.4	 2,725.4	2,221.0</p>
<p> Total loans		   334.5	   334.8	  367.5</p>
<p> Net household savings   2,415.9	 2,382.6	1,853.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are not inflation adjusted. December 1996 and January 1997 figures are preliminary. The consumer price inflation was 18.9 percent year-on-year in January.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042 ($ = 174.3 Hungarian Forints)</p>
